{{Documentation/Header}}
Returns the '''number of pages''' in a category, as a plain integer. Used to build the live counts on [[Utaite Wiki:Utaite List]] and its <code>/Number</code> subpages.

It works by running a DPL query that emits <code>+1</code> per result, prefixing the whole thing with <code>0</code>, and evaluating the sum — so an empty category correctly returns <code>0</code> rather than a blank.

==Syntax==
{{T|ARTICLESINCAT|block=1
|v1=cat =
|v2=titleregexp =
|v3=categoryregexp =
|v4=nottitleregexp =
|v5=cached =
}}

==Examples==
{| class="wikitable"
! Code !! Result
|-
| <code><nowiki>{{ARTICLESINCAT|cat=Male Utaite}}</nowiki></code> || {{ARTICLESINCAT|cat=Male Utaite}}
|-
| <code><nowiki>{{ARTICLESINCAT|cat=Male Utaite|titleregexp=^[0-9]+}}</nowiki></code> || {{ARTICLESINCAT|cat=Male Utaite|titleregexp=^[0-9]+}}
|-
| <code><nowiki>{{ARTICLESINCAT|cat=Male Utaite|titleregexp=(?i)^[z]}}</nowiki></code> || {{ARTICLESINCAT|cat=Male Utaite|titleregexp=(?i)^[z]}}
|}

Prefix a regex with <code>(?i)</code> to make it case-insensitive.

{| class="dataTable sortable"
! Parameter !! Aliases !! Label !! Description !! Type !! Default !! Status
|-
| <code>cat</code> || – || Category || Category to count, without the <code>Category:</code> prefix. || string || – || <span style="color:red;font-weight:bold;">Required</span>
|-
| <code>titleregexp</code> || – || Title regexp || Count only titles matching this regular expression. || string || – ||
|-
| <code>categoryregexp</code> || – || Category regexp || Count only pages whose categories match this regular expression. || string || – ||
|-
| <code>nottitleregexp</code> || – || Exclude title regexp || Exclude titles matching this regular expression. || string || – ||
|-
| <code>cached</code> || – || Allow cached results || Set to <code>true</code> to permit cached DPL results. || string || false ||
|}

{{Notice
| header = Performance
| info = <code>cached</code> defaults to '''false''', so every call runs a fresh query. On a page with many counts, pass <code>cached=true</code> unless the numbers must be exact to the minute.
| border = orange
}}

